%U A175531 1159954316194989017102401,2088144166339753513992001,2196407820059694924883201,3339611018825185787482801,4105879060352839139462401
%N A175531 Carmichael numbers of order 2.
%C A175531 Odd composite integer k is in this sequence if k == 1 or p (mod p^2 - 1) for every prime p|k.
%C A175531 Every term below 10^28 satisfies k == 1 (mod p^2 - 1) for every prime p | k, and no term below 10^28 has a prime factor larger than 209089 (the largest prime factor of a(38)). Howe (2000, Section 5) gives the term 23 * 67 * 71 * 89 * 109 * 113 * 191 * 199 * 233 * 239 * 271 * 307 * 373 * 419 * 521 * 911 * 929 * 1153 * 1217 * 1429 * 2089 * 2729 * 23561 (about 3.92*10^59), for which k == p (mod p^2 - 1) when p = 1153. A smaller such term is 4626955899583332366834728873711784001 = 23 * 37 * 43 * 61 * 79 * 109 * 151 * 193 * 307 * 373 * 727 * 883 * 1871 * 2549 * 23561 (about 4.63*10^36), for which k == p (mod p^2 - 1) when p = 193; it was found by Howe's construction, not by an exhaustive search, so the smallest such term is only known to lie between 10^28 and 4.63*10^36. - _J C Puddefoot_, Oct 07 2026
%H A175531 J C Puddefoot, <a href="/A175531/b175531.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..45</a>
